00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:04.980
In Russian, many travel words change their endings depending on whether you are going

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.820
to a place or already added.

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:09.160
This is the propositional case.

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:13.040
English uses in on or add with the same word.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:19.080
Russian adds endings like E or U, for example, в самолете means in the airplane,

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.760
в поезде means on the train, в отеле means in the hotel.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:28.400
It feels like giving the world a little travel sticker so everyone knows where you are.

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.080
Russian laughs long train journeys across their huge country.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:37.120
The famous Trans-Siberian railway takes 7 days from Moscow to Vladivostok.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:41.420
Families often bring teens next to share with new friends in the compartment,

00:02:41.420 --> 00:02:44.180
турник travel into a warm social adventure.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.760
Now hear something really cool about one of today's words.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.800
Want to know a secret about чемодан?

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:56.000
Did you know that the Russian word чемодан and the French word вализа are cousins from the same journey?

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.020
This word started in Turkish as chanta, meaning back, travel through French, вализа

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:06.180
and finally arrived in Russian in the 18th century as чемодан.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:10.280
But be careful, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine,

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:12.020
but actually means shop.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.320
Next time you see a suitcase, remember it cousins with чемодан.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.520
They both come from a torquish route.

00:03:19.140 --> 00:03:22.340
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.540
Do you remember what bilet means?

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:28.640
Try using дайте мне bilet, пожалуйста, out loud three times,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:30.860
while pretending to hand over your passport.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.300
For kids, draw a big airplane

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:38.000
and label the parts with today's words like Somalot, bilet and Rugsak.

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.260
Молодец, that means well done.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.920
